## 1. Objective
The objective of Day 7 was to understand how Linux manages user identities, group memberships, file ownership, and access permissions.
The exercise involved creating a standard user account, protecting private directories, configuring a shared workspace, and troubleshooting permission-related failures.
The final goal was to configure a directory where authorized users could collaborate without manually adjusting the ownership and permissions of every newly created file.
A final security test verified that unauthorized accounts were denied access.

